2.—(1) In these Regulations —
“authorised officer” means a public officer authorised by the Minister to represent the Minister in any oral hearing;
“authorised representative” means a person authorised by the restrained person to represent the restrained person in any oral hearing;
“file” means to file with the Council;
“parties” means the representor or restrained person (as the case may be) and the Minister, and “party” means either of them;
“recommendation”, in relation to a restraining order, means the Council’s recommendation on the restraining order under section 33(6);
“representations” means representations made under section 33(2) against a restraining order;
“representor”, in relation to representations, means the restrained person;
“restrained person” has the meaning given by section 33(8);
“secretary” means the secretary appointed under paragraph 12 of the Schedule to the Act;
“working day” means any day other than a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday.
(2) The definitions in paragraph 1 of the Schedule to the Act apply to these Regulations.
(3) Unless it is otherwise provided, a reference to a section in these Regulations is a reference to a section in the Act.
